<div id="settings_plugin_Pinput_Shaping">
    <h4>Calibration settings</h4>
    <p>Travel dimensions come from the active OctoPrint printer profile.
        Changes apply to the next calibration session.</p>
    <form class="form-horizontal">
        <div class="control-group">
            <label class="control-label" for="pinput-sensor">Accelerometer</label>
            <div class="controls"><select id="pinput-sensor" data-bind="value: sensorType, disable: busy">
                <option value="adxlspi">ADXL345 SPI</option>
                <option value="adxlusb">ADXL345 USB</option>
                <option value="lis2dw">LIS2DW USB</option>
            </select></div>
        </div>
        <div class="control-group">
            <label class="control-label" for="pinput-port">Sensor serial port</label>
            <div class="controls"><input id="pinput-port" type="text" placeholder="/dev/serial/by-id/..."
                data-bind="value: sensorPort, disable: busy">
                <p class="help-block">USB sensors only. Use a stable device path distinct from the printer port.
                    Blank uses /dev/ttyACM1 for ADXL345 USB or /dev/ttyACM0 for LIS2DW.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="control-group">
            <label class="control-label" for="pinput-channel">Sensor channels</label>
            <div class="controls"><select id="pinput-channel" data-bind="value: sensorAxis, disable: busy">
                <option value="sum">Combined XYZ spectrum</option><option value="x">Sensor X</option>
                <option value="y">Sensor Y</option><option value="z">Sensor Z</option>
            </select><p class="help-block">Combined spectra tolerate different sensor orientations.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="control-group">
            <label class="control-label" for="pinput-accel-min">Start acceleration (mm/s²)</label>
            <div class="controls"><input id="pinput-accel-min" type="number" min="1" data-bind="value: accelMin, disable: busy"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="control-group">
            <label class="control-label" for="pinput-accel-max">Maximum acceleration (mm/s²)</label>
            <div class="controls"><input id="pinput-accel-max" type="number" min="1" data-bind="value: accelMax, disable: busy">
                <p class="help-block">Must fit the reported firmware limit. Step resolution can further limit reachable frequencies.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="control-group">
            <label class="control-label" for="pinput-freq-start">Start frequency (Hz)</label>
            <div class="controls"><input id="pinput-freq-start" type="number" min="5" max="199" data-bind="value: freqStart, disable: busy">
                <p class="help-block">Shaper fitting uses measured frequencies at or above 20 Hz.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="control-group">
            <label class="control-label" for="pinput-freq-end">End frequency (Hz)</label>
            <div class="controls"><input id="pinput-freq-end" type="number" min="21" max="200" data-bind="value: freqEnd, disable: busy"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="control-group">
            <label class="control-label" for="pinput-freq-step">Frequency step (Hz)</label>
            <div class="controls"><input id="pinput-freq-step" type="number" min="0.5" max="10" step="0.5" data-bind="value: freqStep, disable: busy"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="control-group">
            <label class="control-label" for="pinput-band-duration">Time per frequency (s)</label>
            <div class="controls"><input id="pinput-band-duration" type="number" min="0.5" max="3" step="0.5" data-bind="value: bandDuration, disable: busy"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="control-group">
            <label class="control-label" for="pinput-damping">Damping ratio</label>
            <div class="controls"><select id="pinput-damping" data-bind="value: dampingRatio, disable: busy">
                <option value="0.05">0.05</option><option value="0.07">0.07</option>
                <option value="0.1">0.10</option><option value="0.15">0.15</option>
            </select></div>
        </div>
    </form>
    <p>LIS2DW calibration requires a wrapper that preserves precise, strictly increasing acquisition timestamps.
        Captures with rounded or duplicate timestamps are rejected.</p>
</div>

